# Oracle probe (L11.9, ADR 0186) — a container element may be any value, including
# a container. The literal builds, prints, and measures on both backends now (ADR 0238);
# what the compiled leg still refuses is reading one out again — xs[2][1] asks a container
# variable for a slot and then asks that slot for a slot, which is the tagged element read
# roadmap L11.1 still owes. The interpreter and CPython agree on every line.
xs = [1, "a", [2, 3]]
print(xs)
print(len(xs))
print(xs[2][1])
m = {"k": [1], "n": 2}
print(m["k"])
print(m["n"])
